# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in every working copy.
#
# `rustfmt.toml` asks for `newline_style = "Unix"`, so `cargo fmt --all --check` fails
# on a tree with CRLF endings. This file was missing, and a Windows checkout applies
# `core.autocrlf=true` by default: CI rewrote every source file on checkout and the
# Formatting step went red on every push, while the same check passed on a developer
# machine whose working copy happened to be LF already.
#
# `eol=lf` is stated explicitly rather than left to `text=auto`, so the result does not
# depend on the git configuration of whoever clones this. An attribute overrides
# `core.autocrlf`, which is the point.
* text=auto eol=lf
